# Task 4b: cost of fix adapt/liggghts + Neighbor::trigger_build vs legacy fix adapt.
# 27k spheres (r0=1 mm) on a 20 mm lattice (no contacts), skin 1 mm -> trigger threshold 0.5*skin = 0.5 mm.
# vars: mode (none|liggghts|legacy), dr (radius increment per application), nev (application interval), nsteps
atom_style granular
atom_modify map array
boundary p p p
newton off
communicate single vel yes
units si
variable L equal 0.02*30
region dom block 0 ${L} 0 ${L} 0 ${L} units box
create_box 1 dom
region fill block 0.001 ${L} 0.001 ${L} 0.001 ${L} units box
lattice sc 0.02
create_atoms 1 region fill
set group all diameter 0.002 density 2500
velocity all set 0.01 0.02 0.03
neighbor 0.001 bin
neigh_modify delay 0
timestep 1e-5
fix m1 all property/global youngsModulus peratomtype 5.e6
fix m2 all property/global poissonsRatio peratomtype 0.45
fix m3 all property/global coefficientRestitution peratomtypepair 1 0.3
fix m4 all property/global coefficientFriction peratomtypepair 1 0.5
pair_style gran model hertz tangential history
pair_coeff * *
fix integr all nve/sphere
compute rad all property/atom radius
variable rnew atom c_rad+${dr}
variable dnew atom 2.0*(c_rad+${dr})
include in.adapt_${mode}
modify_timing on
thermo 100
run ${nsteps}
